==German==
===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|klette}}, from {{inh|de|goh|kletta|g=f}}, {{m|goh|kletto|g=m}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*gleyt-||to cling to, cleave, stick}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gley-}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|kledda|g=f}}, {{m|osx|kleddo|g=m}} and {{cog|gml|klette}}. Related to {{m|de|klettern||to climb}} and {{m|de|Kleid||dress}}, also {{cog|dum|clisse}}, {{cog|nl|klis}}, {{cog|ang|cliþe}}, {{m|ang|clāte}} and {{cog|en|clote||burdock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈklɛtə/|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|ɛtə|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Kletten}}
# [[burdock]]
# a [[burr]] (a seed pod with sharp features that stick in fur or clothing)
# {{lb|de|figuratively}} a clingy person

